examiner (round 1): approach for tests/lint-ui.test.ts.

One `test` per Proof leg, named for the leg and its Machine clause:
 (a) [M1] root package.json — `scripts["lint:ui"]` exact, one assertion per devDependency name, `@shadcn/lint` exactly `^0.1.0`;
 (b) [M2] eslint.config.mjs exists + text contains `@shadcn/lint`; `node node_modules/eslint/bin/eslint.js --print-config <sample>` exits 0, one assertion per rule id with `[0] === 2`, `shadcn/no-restyle` deep-equal `[2, {allow: ['layout']}]` (plus M3's 'no settings' condition read off the same printed config, tolerantly as `settings ?? {}` deep-equal `{}`);
 (c) [M3] `Bun.spawnSync(['bun','run','lint:ui','-f','json'], {cwd: ROOT})` exits 1, exactly one entry whose filePath ends with `<tmp>/Bad.tsx`, one assertion per rule id over that entry's `messages.map(m => m.ruleId)`;
 (d) [M4] no entry whose filePath contains `<tmp>-bad`;
 (e) [M5] the three fix-wordings — `p-3.25`, `@utility`, `owns its spacing`.

The three temporary files are the Proof's verbatim fences with a random suffix substituted for `<rand>`; they are written once by a lazily-invoked capture that runs both spawns and removes them in a `finally`, so legs (c)–(e) read one recorded run. Both spawns are captured non-throwing (exit code + stdout + stderr kept) so a BASE red reads as 'the script/config is not there', not as a JSON parse error.

At BASE node_modules has no eslint, no @shadcn/lint, no tailwindcss and package.json has no lint:ui — the exam is red for exactly that.
